\ A `with-parameter` whose body produces a value consumed by a following
\ instruction compiles under runtime-image AOT: the body's row-variable output
\ collapses the abstract stack to a row region, so the consumer compiles above
\ it instead of failing NC.5 the way it did when with-parameter abandoned
\ compilation. These results come from the compiled path and match the
\ interpreter: a value-producing body printed after the binding ends, nested
\ bindings that restore the outer value and then the default, and fresh
\ per-invocation state across two calls to the same word.
wp: parameter{ [ 0 ] } ;

\ Bind wp to 99; the body reads it and produces it; the `.` after with-parameter
\ consumes the produced value.
99 wp [ wp get ] with-parameter .
"---" print-line

\ Nested dynamic scope: the inner binding is active inside, the outer value is
\ restored after the inner binding ends, and the default returns once both end.
1 wp [
  2 wp [ wp get ] with-parameter .
  wp get .
] with-parameter
wp get .
"---" print-line

\ Fresh per-invocation state: the same binding-and-producing word called twice
\ with different values yields independent results.
bind-show: ( n -- ) [ wp [ wp get 1 + ] with-parameter . ] ;
5 bind-show
10 bind-show
